{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"whacky-cadaverous-coati","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Symptom\nCI-only flake in `tests/unit/test_authorship_batched_ticket_map_7084.py::test_fixture_batched_map_recovers_from_one_transient_git_read[rc128]`. Observed on Gerrit change 1837 ps3 (GH run 32032700192, ubuntu py3.12, xdist worker popen-gw1):\n\n    assert batched[position] == authorship.resolve_event_commit(position, ticket_dir)\n    E  AssertionError: assert 'c7c2f6...' == None\n    E   where None = resolve_event_commit('1002-bbbb1111', '.../aaaa-bbbb-cccc-dddd')\n\n## Root cause\nThe equivalence assertion compares two resolvers over the same fixture git history:\n- batched side (`_fixture_batched_map` -> `build_ticket_position_commit_map`) is wrapped in a 5-attempt transient-recovery loop in the test.\n- oracle side (`src/rebar/attest/authorship_resolution.py::resolve_event_commit`) is documented fail-closed: 'Any failure - git non-zero, no match, git missing, a timeout, or any exception - yields None; this function NEVER raises.' It has NO transient retry.\n\nWhen a transient git object-store read hits the *oracle* call in CI, it returns None while the batched side has already recovered, so the assertion fails. This is exactly the git-read-transient class the file's own forensics/transient infra (bugs innovative-dandruffy-deer, warmthless-dermal-oropendola) was built to diagnose - but only the batched side was hardened.\n\n## Evidence it is environmental / not a code regression\n- Deterministically PASSES locally: 5/5 in isolation, 12/12 x3 under xdist -n auto.\n- Unrelated to the change it surfaced on (RP-01 S4 = LLM structured-output tracing; this is the authorship subsystem).\n- S1-S3 of the same stack passed this test at Verified+1.\n\n## Fix direction (not done here)\nWrap the oracle side of the equivalence assertion in the same bounded transient-retry the batched side uses (or give `resolve_event_commit` an internal bounded retry for transient rc!=0/OSError, keeping the fail-closed contract for a genuine no-match). Do NOT retry-until-green in CI.","id":"f94e-cf09-fed7-422d","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Flaky: test_fixture_batched_map_recovers oracle side (resolve_event_commit) not transient-hardened"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786973077119689001,"uuid":"aecd2b0b-23ce-4d3a-ba45-614524d41e57"}